{number: 132}
{title: Glorious Things of Thee Are Spoken}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Glorious things of [Bb] thee are [F] spoken,
[C7] Zion, city [F] of our God;
He whose word can-[Bb] not be [F] broken
[C7] Formed thee for His [F] own abode:
On the [C7] Rock of [F] Ages founded,
[C7] What can shake thy [F] sure repose?
With sal-[F] vation's [Bb] walls sur-[F] rounded,
Thou may'st [C7] smile at all thy [F] foes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] See, the streams of [Bb] living [F] waters,
[C7] Springing from e-[F] ternal love,
Well supply thy [Bb] sons and [F] daughters,
And [C7] all fear of [F] want remove:
Who can [C7] faint while [F] such a river
[C7] Ever flows their [F] thirst to assuage?
Grace which, [F] like the [Bb] Lord, the [F] Giver,
Never [C7] fails from age to [F] age.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Round each habi-[Bb] tation [F] hov'ring,
[C7] See the cloud and [F] fire appear
For a glory [Bb] and a [F] cov'ring,
[C7] Showing that the [F] Lord is near!
Glorious [C7] things of [F] thee are spoken,
[C7] Zion, city [F] of our God;
He whose [F] word can-[Bb] not be [F] broken
Formed thee [C7] for His own a-[F] bode.
{end_of_verse}
